WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:03.111
(crowd chatter)

00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:04.485
- Ahh.

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:07.729
(choking noises)

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:08.863
- Sorry.

00:00:09.463 --> 00:00:10.592
Sorry.

00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:12.754
I didn't see you there.

00:00:12.754 --> 00:00:17.662
("Ranz des Vaches" from "William
Tell Overture" by Rossini)

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.038
That didn't last.

00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:25.779
- Hey, how's that project coming?

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:27.858
I really need it end of day today.

00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:30.050
- I'll give it my full attention.

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:32.770
- You switched off your computer.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.639
What's wrong?

00:00:33.639 --> 00:00:34.634
- Nothing.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.122
I'm all right.

00:00:36.522 --> 00:00:38.711
- Okay, the end of day buddy.

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:45.091
- Lap it up, fuzz ball.

00:00:45.091 --> 00:00:46.706
Yes Crunchy.

00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:48.320
I know the transmission's broken.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.303
(dog barks)

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:53.102
- Oh Doritos.

00:00:53.102 --> 00:00:54.333
Can I get one?

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.818
- These are not the
chips you're looking for.

00:00:56.818 --> 00:00:58.222
- No, I love nacho cheese.

00:00:58.222 --> 00:01:00.050
They're my favorite.

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:03.673
- These are not the favorite
thing you're looking for.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.780
(loud breathing noises)

00:01:17.356 --> 00:01:18.760
- Oh my god.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.180
You're breath.

00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:26.616
- Dammit.

00:01:26.616 --> 00:01:28.190
- Yes.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.130
Give in to your hate.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:34.574
Give in to your anger.

00:01:34.574 --> 00:01:37.014
- What are you getting
Dad for his birthday?

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:38.089
Do you think it's weird

00:01:38.089 --> 00:01:40.197
that he calls me his little princess?

00:01:41.864 --> 00:01:43.644
I was thinking of getting
him a Kindle Fire.

00:01:43.644 --> 00:01:45.264
I feel like he could
really benefit from that.

00:01:45.264 --> 00:01:46.768
What, no.

00:01:47.758 --> 00:01:49.156
(disgust noise)

00:01:50.326 --> 00:01:52.142
God, Jesus.

00:01:53.251 --> 00:01:54.123
Not again.

00:01:54.123 --> 00:01:54.969
- There's a lot to explain,

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:58.242
but I think it's best
if you just watch this.

00:01:58.766 --> 00:02:03.676
(majestic brass music)

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.145
- Why?

